ous characteristics rather he is the  blank middle they fill in he is an  opening a vacant unclaimed potentiality  rather than an ontologically assignable  identity and so we get to fill bond's  famed tuxedo with whoever we need him to  be at that moment in history his  adventures have adapted to our changing  taste with the campy gadget-filled  iterations of the 90s giving way to the  grittier more grounded style of the  2000s we were expecting an exploding pen  we don't really go in for that anymore  as a result bond is able to retain his  appeal from one decade to the next even  his taste and trends change completely  with a new incarnation of the character  arriving tailor-made to meet each  audience's demands but what do you guys  think will there eventually come a day  where james bond simply has to be put  into retirement or is he such a potent  impliable symbol that we can keep  reinventing him forever let us know in  the comments thanks as always to our  patrons for all your support and  remember to check out our podcast  wrestle that subscribe button like it's  a pre-cgi shark and don't forget to ring  that bell and as always thanks for  watching later  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]

